column234:
23/Oct/25 1:27 PM;ndavis2;Had brief phone discussion with Miles Ibarra from AMC. They found that there would be a ~3V voltage drop on the 23.25ft (46.5ft round trip) and 14awg cable and ~1.25V-1.5V drop on the 10.50ft (21ft round trip) 14awg cable.

At a high level the goal would be to reduce the cable resistance such that we may only have a *0.5V** voltage drop. AMC requests that we may look into how flexible our cable specifications can be in terms of reducing cable routing (length), adjustment to cable gauge or even additional wiring to accommodate for the wire resistance.

Further internal discussion required.;;;

